WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Brakes and ABS. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Explain wheel-speed sensing and pressure modulation

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: ABS uses wheel-speed information and controlled brake pressure to help manage wheel slip during braking. It is a feedback system, not a shorter-stopping guarantee on every surface.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: Sensor → controller estimate → hydraulic pressure adjustment → new wheel-speed measurement.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Control-loop ordering

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Ideal mechanism only; friction, heat and part-specific behavior need measurements.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Explain wheel-speed sensing and pressure modulation
